WHAT WAS BUILT:
1. RefreshToken Prisma model with familyId for reuse detection,
   tokenHash (SHA-256), revokedAt, expiresAt.
2. EmailVerification and PasswordReset models added to schema.
3. TokenService: Generates cryptographically secure tokens,
   hashes with SHA-256, provides verification and reset token
   generators with appropriate TTLs (24h email, 1h reset).
4. MailService: Sends verification and password reset emails.
   Logs to console in dev, placeholder for Resend/Postmark in prod.
5. AuthService fully rewritten:
   - register(): Creates tenant+user in $transaction, issues
     verification email, returns token pair.
   - login(): Validates credentials, issues token pair.
   - refreshTokens(): Validates refresh token hash, checks for
     reuse (revokes entire family on reuse), issues new pair.
   - logout(): Revokes single session or all sessions.
   - verifyEmail(): Validates and marks token as used.
   - forgotPassword(): Generates reset token, sends email.
   - resetPassword(): Validates token, hashes new password,
     revokes all existing refresh tokens.
   - setAuthCookies(): Sets httpOnly/Secure/SameSite=Strict
     cookies for access (15m) and refresh (7d) tokens.
   - clearAuthCookies(): Clears cookies on logout.
6. AuthController: New endpoints:
   - POST /auth/refresh (cookie-based)
   - POST /auth/logout (revokes + clears cookies)
   - POST /auth/verify-email
   - POST /auth/forgot-password (rate-limited 3/min)
   - POST /auth/reset-password (rate-limited 5/min)
7. Frontend:
   - ApiClient class in packages/shared for typed API calls
     with credentials: 'include' for cookie support.
   - Zustand store updated with real login/register/logout/fetchProfile.
   - Login page: Real API calls with error display, no hardcoded creds.
   - Register page: Real API calls, error handling.
   - Forgot Password page with success state.
   - Reset Password page with token from URL.
   - Verify Email page with token validation.
   - Next.js middleware: protects /app/* routes, redirects
     authenticated users away from auth pages.
   - AppShell: fetches profile on mount, shows loading state,
     redirects to login if unauthenticated.
   - Header: Shows real user name/initials/role, real logout.
   - .env.example created for both apps.

